Jenkins :
=========
--> Jenkins is an open-source Automation Tool for CI and CD.

--> Jenkins Developed using Java.

--> Jenkins is part of Hudson Project.

--> Initial it is called as Hudson, Then later it was renamed as Jenkins.

Installation :
==============
--> Jenkins Installation in Linux Machine means, First to check Java Installed or Not.

    $ java -version
    $ javac -version

--> If not Installed Java in your Machine Then, First Install Java

    $ sudo dnf/yum install java-21-openjdk-devel
    
    $ sudo dnf/yum install java-17-openjdk-devel

--> Since you're learning Jenkins, Maven, Tomcat, and Java for DevOps, Below mention which version is suitable or best working.

--> Learn Java 17 if you're working with older enterprise projects, as many companies still use it.

--> Learn Java 21 for new projects because it's the newer LTS release with modern features and performance improvements.


--> After Java Installation Successfull, Go to add Jenkins Repository to your YUM Repository in Jenkins Machines
  
   $ sudo wget -O /etc/yum.repos.d/jenkins.repo \
    https://pkg.jenkins.io/rpm-stable/jenkins.repo

--> Update All Packages
   
   $ sudo yum upgrade

--> Now Install Jenkins

   $ sudo yum install jenkins

--> To Enable Jenkins step by step using below commands :

   $ sudo systemctl daemon-reload

   $ sudo systemctl enable jenkins

   $ sudo systemctl start jenkins

   $ sudo systemctl status jenkins

--> Go to your AWS Console then copy your ec2 public ip, then paste ur your browser :

   Open Browser and write your ip <public-ip>:8080/ 
   (Like : 13.127.30.171:8080/)

   :8080 is a Jenkins default port no., so u must add in ur ip.

--> Put this ip, showing Jenkins server and also ask Jenkins Admin Password, Go to jenkins linux machine to write below command
 
   $ sudo cat /var/lib/jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword

   --> Copy the password and paste in Jenkins Server.

--> After, Then click on Install Suggested Plugins and set admin username, password.

Issues :
========
--> Once AWS ec2 stopped jenkins Instance, Again start server then Public IP must be changed. Jenkins prevoius ip and aws new ip doesn't match, so Jenkin server almost run but it's running very slow. To overcome this problem used below command

   $ sudo vi /var/lib/jenkins/jenkins.model.JenkinsLocationConfiguration.xml
    
--> Only for public ip changed, and save. Again restart jenkins.

How to change Jenkins port number:
==================================
1.Go to root directory
2.Go to /etc/sysconfig
3.Open Jenkins file and change Jenkins port number
4.Restart Jenkins server


If we Forgot Jenkins Password, Then how to recover it ?
=======================================================
1.Go to /var/lib/jenkins/config.xml
2.Set Value for userSecurity as false
  ex: <userSecurity>false</userSecurity>
3.Restart Jenkins and try to access.


















